-- title:
--   Commuting class-set Hecke matrices at coprime indices
-- statement:
--   Fix $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda$ of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of the project's predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, and it is finitely generated. Write $U=$ [`Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer Λ`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L26) for the stabiliser, inside the units of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$, of the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ an integral finite adèle; the class set `ClassSet U` is the double coset quotient of the unit group by the image of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^{\times}$ under the diagonal embedding on the left and by $U$ on the right, assumed here to be a finite type with decidable equality. Let $\ell,\ell'$ be coprime natural numbers, and let $T,T'$ be sets of finite idelic units with $T\subseteq$ `primeHeckeSet Λ ℓ` and $T'\subseteq$ `primeHeckeSet Λ ℓ'`, i.e. each $h\in T$ satisfies $h\in\widehat{\Lambda}$, $\ell h^{-1}\in\widehat{\Lambda}$, $h^{-1}\notin\widehat{\Lambda}$ and $\ell^{-1}h\notin\widehat{\Lambda}$ (with $\ell'$ in place of $\ell$ for $T'$), where $\widehat{\Lambda}$ denotes the above adelic box. Assume further that $T$ and $T'$ are stable under multiplication by elements of $U$ on the left and on the right, and that the image of each of $T$, $T'$ in the coset space of the unit group modulo $U$ is finite. The conclusion is that the two integer matrices [`CerednikDrinfeld.classSetHeckeMatrix U T`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_ClassSetGraph.html#L33) and [`CerednikDrinfeld.classSetHeckeMatrix U T'`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_ClassSetGraph.html#L33), indexed by `ClassSet U` and having $(i,j)$ entry the cardinality of the incidence set `HeckeIncidence U T` (respectively for $T'$) formed from a chosen representative of the class $j$ and the class $i$, commute.
--
--   This is the commutativity of Brandt matrices, or of the Hecke operators on the class set $\mathbb{H}^{\times}\backslash\widehat{\mathbb{H}}^{\times}/\widehat{\Lambda}^{\times}$ of a quaternion order, at coprime indices. It feeds into [`CerednikDrinfeld.classSetHeckeLaws_of_isEichlerOrder_meetOrder`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.classSetHeckeLaws_of_isEichlerOrder_meetOrder), where the Hecke matrices attached to an Eichler order are shown to satisfy the expected relations.
